<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.01 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.01 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0380 to the dollar, up from 3.0400 on Monday and at 1.8125 to the mark, up from 1.8145, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.01 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Monday's 2.93 percent fix. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
